# The octoflow-gate release that judges this repo's changes, as ci/fetch-gate.sh reads it: one line, the release's
# version and the sha256 of its octoflow-gate-<version>.tar.gz, as the release's .sha256 asset gives it. scripts/gate
# reads this file from the judge's commit, so a change to it judges the changes after it, never itself. Raise it to a
# new release only after that release exists and has been checked (sha256sum -c on the downloaded tarball). The
# release named here must read this commit's gate.toml, which scripts/gate checks, and be 0.7.0 or later: scripts/gate
# runs no release before the first that ships `gate`, so a rollback below 0.7.0 is a revert of scripts/gate too.
